// MQ-9 Reaper wing + body lift and drag - the whole aircraft, per its main
// wings' reference area (both together - each wing uses it on its half).
// Illustrative, derived from the Reaper's shape with standard aerodynamics,
// NOT official data:
// - a long, slender, straight wing (about 20 m span, aspect ratio ~17):
//   3D lift slope ~0.095/deg (2 pi A / (2 + sqrt(A^2 + 4)) - close to a 2D
//   airfoil's, unlike the F-16's stubby wing);
// - a strongly cambered, high-lift airfoil: CL 0.35 at 0 deg;
// - no strake vortex lift - a conventional stall: CL peaks ~1.45 at 14 deg
//   and drops off sharply, ~1.0 by 20 deg; negative side peaks ~-0.80 at
//   -14 deg;
// - drag: profile ~0.022 (whole aircraft - fuselage, sensor ball, V-tail)
//   + induced 0.023 CL^2 (1 / (pi A e), A ~17, e ~0.8 - about a fifth of the
//   F-16's, which is how it loiters for a day), plus a separation rise
//   through the stall, turning into flat-plate drag (1.25 sin^2 alpha) out
//   to 90 deg; lift past the stall follows the flat-plate shape too.
// Evenly spaced at 1 deg. Regenerate rather than hand-edit.
